1
00:04:13,636 --> 00:04:19,636
This Thanksgiving, carve out some family time.

2
00:08:27,272 --> 00:08:33,272
Flesh & Blood is a horror, thriller film directed by Patrick Lussier.

3
00:12:40,909 --> 00:12:46,909
Kimberly, a teenager suffering from agoraphobia, has not left
the house since her mother's unsolved murder.

4
00:16:54,545 --> 00:17:00,545
On the eve of Thanksgiving, she begins to suspect that the safe harbor
of home and her doting father may be a dangerous mirage.

5
00:21:08,181 --> 00:21:14,181
Kimberly Tooms, played by Diana Silvers.

6
00:25:21,818 --> 00:25:27,818
Henry Tooms, played by Dermot Mulroney.

7
00:29:35,454 --> 00:29:41,454
Dr. Helen Saunders, played by Tembi Locke.

8
00:33:49,090 --> 00:33:55,090
Rose Tooms, played by Meredith Salenger.

9
00:38:02,727 --> 00:38:08,727
Officer Foster, played by Lavetta Cannon.

10
00:42:16,363 --> 00:42:22,363
Officer Banks, played by Heidi Sulzman.

11
00:46:30,000 --> 00:46:36,000
Flesh and Blood is a 1985 erotic historical adventure film directed by Paul Verhoeven, and starring Rutger Hauer,
Jennifer Jason Leigh, Tom Burlinson, Susan Tyrrell, Ronald Lacey, Bruno Kirby and Jack Thompson.

12
00:50:43,636 --> 00:50:49,636
The script was written by Verhoeven and Gerard Soeteman.

13
00:54:57,272 --> 00:55:03,272
The story is set in 1501 in early modern Italy, and follows two warring
groups of mercenaries and their longstanding quarrel.

14
00:59:10,909 --> 00:59:16,909
The script is partly based on unused material for the Dutch television series
Floris, which was the debut for Verhoeven, Soeteman and Hauer.

15
01:03:24,545 --> 01:03:30,545
The film, originally titled God's Own Butchers, was also known
as The Rose and the Sword on early VHS releases.

16
01:07:38,181 --> 01:07:44,181
It was Verhoeven's first English-language film.

17
01:11:51,818 --> 01:11:57,818
Upon its release in August 1985, Flesh and Blood was a box office bomb,
earning only US$100,000 on a US$6.5 million production budget.

18
01:16:05,454 --> 01:16:11,454
The film has since garnered a small cult following.

19
01:20:19,090 --> 01:20:25,090
The director's biographer called it "a crucial Verhoeven film, because the fight between logic and spirituality is one
that is very familiar to the director; these are the elements still fighting for priority in his own mind."

20
01:24:32,727 --> 01:24:38,727
The film explores themes of therapist, holiday,
thanksgiving, murder, agoraphobia.

21
01:28:46,363 --> 01:28:52,363
The tone is dark and intense.
